#  OPTIONS:
# 
#  -i <iface>      Network device <iface> (default: eth0).
#  -r <file>       Read pcap <file>.
#  -l <file>       Name of the logfile (default: /var/log/passivedns.log).
#  -L <file>       Name of NXDOMAIN logfile (default: /var/log/passivedns.log).
#  -b 'BPF'        Berkley Packet Filter.
#                  Default keeps port 53, IPv4 fragments, and IPv6
#                  extension headers (hop-by-hop, routing, fragment,
#                  destination options).
#  -p <file>       Name of pid file (default: /var/run/passivedns.pid).
#  -s <bytes>      Live snapshot length (default: 4096, 0 means 262144).
#                  A longer frame is truncated. On the capture device:
#                  ethtool -K <iface> gro off
#  --stats-file <file>  Write SIGUSR1 stats to this file.
#  -S <mem>        Soft memory limit in MB (default: 256).
#  -C <sec>        Seconds to cache DNS objects in memory (default 43200).
#  -P <sec>        Seconds between printing duplicate DNS info (default 86400).
#  -X <flags>      Manually set DNS RR Types to care about(Default -X 46CDNPRShV).
#  -u <uid>        User ID to drop privileges to.
#  -g <gid>        Group ID to drop privileges to.
#  -T <dir>        Directory to chroot into.
#  -D              Run as daemon.
#  -V              Show version and exit.
#  -h              This help message.
# 
#  FLAGS:
# 
#   4:A    6:AAAA  C:CNAME  D:DNAME  N:NAPTR  O:SOA
#   P:PTR  R:RP    S:SRV    T:TXT    M:MX     n:NS
#   h:HTTPS V:SVCB
#   x:NXD  0:NOERR (empty answer)
# 
## Default values
NAME=passivedns
PIDFILE=/var/run/passivedns.pid
DAEMON=/usr/bin/$NAME

## Quick and dirty:
INTERFACE="-i eth0"
LOGFILE="-l /var/log/passivedns.log"
NXLOGFILE="-L /var/log/passivedns-nx.log"
LOGSYSLOG=""
NXSYSLOG=""
MAXMEM="-S 256"
PRINT="-P 86400"
RRTYPES="-X 46CDNOPRSTMnxhV"
# Drop is fail-closed: if -u or -g names an account that does not exist,
# passivedns exits. Leave these commented until that account exists.
# Bash treats UID as readonly, so the option variable is DROPUSER.
#DROPUSER="-u passivedns"
#DROPGROUP="-g passivedns"
#CHROOT="-T /usr/lib/passivedns"
DEAMON="-D"
ARGS="$INTERFACE $LOGFILE $NXLOGFILE $LOGSYSLOG $NXSYSLOG $MAXMEM $PRINT $RRTYPES $DROPUSER $DROPGROUP $CHROOT $DEAMON"
